### tests/category.http
### Prerequisites: server running on localhost:8080, DB migrated and reachable.
### Run tests top to bottom - some depend on state created by earlier ones (marked below).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

# =========================================================
# GetCategoriesHandler - GET /categories
# =========================================================

### 1. List all categories - happy path
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories

# Expected: 200 OK, body: {"categories": [...]}  (or [] if DB is empty)


# =========================================================
# CreateCategoryHandler - POST /categories
# =========================================================

### 2. Create category - happy path
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Electronics",
  "slug": "electronics",
  "description": "Gadgets and consumer electronics"
}

### Expected: 201 Created, body: {"category": {"uuid": "...", "name": "Electronics", ...}}
# Save the returned uuid - it's used in tests 8, 9, 12 below.


### 3. Create category - malformed JSON body
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Broken", "slug": }

### Expected: 400 Bad Request, body: {"error": "invalid request body"}


### 4. Create category - empty name (validation error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "slug": "empty-name-test",
  "description": "test"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request, body: {"error": "category is invalid", "error_description": "..."}


### 5. Create category - name too long (>100 chars, validation error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA",
  "slug": "too-long-name-test",
  "description": "test"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request, body: {"error": "category is invalid", "error_description": "..."}


### 6. Create category - duplicate name/slug (must run AFTER test 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Electronics",
  "slug": "electronics",
  "description": "Duplicate attempt"
}

### Expected: 409 Conflict, body: {"error": "category already exists"}


# =========================================================
# GetCategoryHandler - GET /categories/{uuid}
# =========================================================

### 7. Get category by UUID - happy path (replace with a real UUID from test 2 response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

# Expected: 200 OK, body: {"category": {...}}


### 8. Get category - invalid UUID format
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/not-a-valid-uuid

# Expected: 400 Bad Request, body: {"error": "category not found"}
# NOTE: consider changing this error message to "invalid category id" for clarity - see comment above.


### 9. Get category - valid UUID, does not exist
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Expected: 404 Not Found, body: {"error": "category not found"}


# =========================================================
# UpdateCategoryHandler - PATCH /categories/{uuid}
# =========================================================

### 10. Update category - happy path (replace with a real UUID from test 2 response)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/categories/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Electronics & Gadgets",
  "slug": "electronics-gadgets",
  "description": "Updated description"
}

### Expected: 200 OK, body: {"category": {"name": "Electronics & Gadgets", ...}}


### 11. Update category - invalid UUID format
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/categories/not-a-valid-uuid
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Doesn't matter",
  "slug": "doesnt-matter",
  "description": "test"
}

### Expected (after bugfix above): 400 Bad Request, body: {"error": "invalid category id"}


### 12. Update category - empty body / validation error
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/categories/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "slug": "",
  "description": ""
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request, body: {"error": "category is invalid", "error_description": "..."}


### 13. Update category - UUID does not exist
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/categories/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ghost Category",
  "slug": "ghost-category",
  "description": "test"
}

### Expected: 404 Not Found, body: {"error": "category not found"}


### 14. Update category - name conflicts with another existing category
# First create a second category to conflict with:
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Books",
  "slug": "books",
  "description": "test"
}

### 14b. Now try renaming category from test 2/10 to "Books" (replace UUID accordingly)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/categories/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Books",
  "slug": "books",
  "description": "conflict attempt"
}

### Expected: 409 Conflict, body: {"error": "duplicate name"}


# =========================================================
# DeleteCategoryHandler - DELETE /categories/{uuid}
# =========================================================

### 15. Delete category - invalid UUID format
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/categories/not-a-valid-uuid

# Expected (after bugfix above): 400 Bad Request, body: {"error": "invalid category id"}


### 16. Delete category - UUID does not exist
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/categories/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Expected: 404 Not Found, body: {"error": "category not found"}


### 17. Delete category - happy path (replace with a real UUID, e.g. the "Books" category from test 14)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/categories/22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

# Expected: 204 No Content, empty body


### 18. Verify deletion - getting the same UUID should now 404 (or still 200 if it's a soft delete without filtering)
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

# Expected: depends on whether DeleteCategory is soft or hard delete - see note below.